From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaszhongsj <lucaszhongsj@foxmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:43:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ios: the framework project compiles the companion as C++20
 too

The framework's own project template (project-framework.yml) is the one the
ACNH build uses, and it kept Xcode's default C++ standard: the app target's
setting alone left std::span undefined there.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: the iOS framework project needs C++20 for eden_duo's headers (std::span); the app target's setting does not reach it
Issue: none yet: no upstream issue for the companion

---
 dm/ios/project-framework.yml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/dm/ios/project-framework.yml b/dm/ios/project-framework.yml
index b9399418..26dad40f 100644
--- a/dm/ios/project-framework.yml
+++ b/dm/ios/project-framework.yml
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ configFiles:     # Generated by build_ipa.sh: embedded-segment link flags + head
 settings:
   base:
     DM_NS_TAG: $(PRODUCT_NAME)
+    CLANG_CXX_LANGUAGE_STANDARD: gnu++20   # the companion's reader is C++20: eden_duo's headers use std::span (dm/third_party/eden_duo/acnh/acnh_bytes.h)
 targets:
   DmIOS:
     type: application
